[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61576,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous cystadenoma and adenofibroma are benign tumours with gastrointestinal or M&uuml;llerian-type mucinous epithelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61577,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8470/0 Mucinous cystadenoma NOS</p>\r\n<p>9015/0 Mucinous adenofibroma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61578,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F32.Y &amp; XH6H73 Other specified benign neoplasm of ovary &amp; Mucinous cystadenoma NOS</p>\r\n<p>2F32.Y &amp; XH59X8 Other specified benign neoplasm of ovary &amp; Mucinous adenofibroma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61579,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61580,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61581,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are localized in the ovary; similar tumours can be found in the retroperitoneum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61582,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common symptoms are abdominal or pelvic pain and symptoms related to an abdominal or pelvic mass. Rarely, patients present with estrogenic or androgenic manifestations secondary to stromal luteinization {15626914}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61583,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are seen in patients over a wide age range (median age: 50&nbsp;years). Benign mucinous neoplasms account for approximately 80% of all primary ovarian mucinous tumours. Mucinous cystadenomas are far more common than adenofibromas {15626914; 2983869}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61584,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61585,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The association of some of these tumours with dermoid cysts suggests a germ cell origin. Some arise in association with Brenner tumours {18976011}. <em>KRAS</em> mutations are found in a significant number of tumours {9118042}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61586,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous cystadenomas are usually unilateral (95%) and multilocular with a smooth outer surface. They range in size from a few centimetres to &gt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;cm (mean size: 10&nbsp;cm). Adenofibromas are usually smaller, predominantly solid, and punctuated with small cysts {15626914; 31097115}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61587,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Mucinous cystadenomas are composed of multiple cysts and glands lined by simple non-stratified mucinous epithelium resembling M&uuml;llerian, gastric foveolar-type, or intestinal epithelium containing goblet cells and sometimes neuroendocrine cells or Paneth cells. Rare simple papillae may be seen. Adenofibromas have small cysts and glands embedded in a prominent fibromatous stroma. Nuclei are small and basally located without cytological atypia, with absent or minimal mitotic activity and apoptotic bodies. The adjacent stroma may be cellular and show luteinization. Focal extravasated mucin or mucinous granulomas may be present secondary to cyst rupture. A component of dermoid cyst or Brenner tumour may be found. Rarely, mucinous cystadenomas can contain mural nodules (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/19\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Mucinous borderline tumour</em>) {16340150; 498013; 9886181} or be associated with clear cell carcinoma {11265180; 17867264; 19851211}, large cell neuroendocrine carcinoma {8786207}, endometrioid carcinoma {14571433}, and sex cord&ndash;stromal tumour {3754727; 15968196}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-09T15:02:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61588,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal washings in benign mucinous ovarian tumours often yield negative cytology or sometimes reactive atypia of mesothelial cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61589,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61590,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tumour with cysts and glands lined by benign mucinous epithelium with no architectural complexity or cytological atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61591,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61592,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 16,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are benign; however, recurrences may be seen after cystectomy or rupture and spillage of the contents {17100827; 20022314}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T14:45:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]